      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "A roof in Utah generally lasts between\n\n15 and 30 years for standard asphalt shingles, though alternative materials can last for 50 to 100 years or more.",
        "snippet_highlighted_words": [
          "between 15 and 30 years for standard asphalt shingles, though alternative materials can last for 50 to 100 years or more"
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          0
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "Utah's intense UV rays, heavy winter snow loads, and rapid freeze-thaw cycles often push real-world performance toward the lower end of manufacturer estimates.",
        "reference_indexes": [
          1,
          2
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Lifespan by Roof Material in Utah"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "3-Tab Asphalt Shingles: 12 to 20 years. These thinner shingles degrade faster under high summer heat and heavy winds."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Architectural (Dimensional) Shingles:\n20 to 30 years. These thicker, higher-quality shingles handle Utah storms and snow much better."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Impact-Resistant Shingles: 30 to 40 years. Designed to better withstand severe hail and flying debris."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Metal Roofing:\n40 to 70 years. Standing seam and steel panels shed heavy mountain snow easily and resist severe weather."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Tile and Slate Roofing: 50 to 100+ years. Extremely durable against sun and fire, though heavy framing is required."
          }
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          3,
          4,
          5,
          6,
          7,
          8
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Climate Factors That Shorten Roof Life in Utah"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Temperature Swings: Utah experiences freezing winter nights and scorching summer afternoons. This constant expansion and contraction cracks and ages materials quickly."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "High UV Exposure:\nIntense high-altitude sun bakes the oils out of asphalt shingles, making them brittle."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Snow and Ice: Heavy winter buildup can lead to ice dams, trapping water under edges and forcing leaks into the decking."
          }
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          9
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "If you want to check your roof's health, tell me:"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "What is your current roof made of?"
          },
          {
            "snippet": "How old is the roof right now?"
          }
        ]
